nodecode-fallback is a rewrite of tomkubik's tomkubik/hermes-fallback:

  https://github.com/tomkubik/hermes-fallback
  commit ce150572ea10de682a2c67902b314590b55683b3
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Tom Kubik (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the heuristic itself. The original's filters and ranking strategies
(parameter count, context window, release recency, flash tier, free tier, tool
calls, provider preference and order) are reimplemented in Common Lisp over the
models Nodecode's own catalog and providers name, and its writing of Hermes'
`fallback_providers` entries became writing Nodecode's `failover.chain`, the key
the engine already walks after a failed round. `fallback_resolve`,
`fallback_apply`, `fallback_status` and `/fallback` are the rewrite of its four
tools and its slash command.

Left out, and why: the interactive first-launch wizard and its live scan of
which providers offer free models (a conversation in Nodecode already does
that, and the cell answers `fallback:providers` without needing one); the
OpenRouter and Nous Portal catalog fetches (Nodecode's own models.dev cache is
the catalog here, and an id's own numbers answer first); the per-request
middleware that rewrote a Hermes request's model mid-flight (Nodecode moves the
whole round onto a chain entry, so there is nothing per-request to rewrite);
and the `switch` verb that rewrote the primary model in Hermes' config, since
this cell picks a fallback and leaves the primary alone.
